From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 10:11:07 +0200
Subject: net: lantiq: tmu: remove the blocks a configuration symbol never
 defined

Nine blocks of the traffic manager were guarded on a configuration
symbol that no Kconfig file in this tree has ever offered: a mock
register shim, a value table it read, four self-tests exercising the
initialisation ordering against that shim, and their initcall
dispatcher. The symbol cannot be set, so none of it has ever been
compiled, let alone run.

Its near-namesake, which did exist, was the symbol that used to build
this whole directory and was removed when the vendor suite went. Keeping
a guard whose only remaining property is that it is always false leaves
five hundred lines that no build can reach and no reader can trust.

Remove the guarded blocks, and with them the statistics reset that only
the self-tests called and the two counter helpers behind it. Two unused
helpers in the buffer manager's header go the same way.

With this, no function under drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq is unreachable
from an entry point.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5-1
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

